<main>

<section class="hero">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="eyebrow">
      PUBLIC RECORDS
    </div>

    <h1>
      FROM THE RECORDS
    </h1>

    <p class="lead">
      These findings come from records involving Lee's Summit's use
      of Flock technology. Wherever possible, the original document
      is provided so you can read the source yourself.
    </p>

  </div>

</section>


<section class="record-section" id="permits">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="record-label">
      RECORD 01
    </div>

    <h2>
      RIGHT-OF-WAY PERMITS
    </h2>

    <p class="record-intro">
      City of Lee's Summit Public Works permits involving Flock ALPR
      installations within public right-of-way.
    </p>


    <div class="permit-grid">

      <article class="document-card">

        <div class="date">
          DECEMBER 20, 2023
        </div>

        <h3>
          31-CAMERA RIGHT-OF-WAY PROJECT
        </h3>

        <div class="meta">
          Permit PRPWRW20236558
        </div>

        <p>
          Project address listed as 908 NW Pryor Rd.
          The permit states that Flock Safety and the Lee's Summit
          Police Department were seeking permits to place 31
          solar-powered ALPR cameras in Lee's Summit right-of-way.
        </p>

        <a
          class="document-button"
          href="/documents/permits/31-camera-row-project-2023.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          VIEW ORIGINAL PERMIT
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="document-card">

        <div class="date">
          JANUARY 5, 2024
        </div>

        <h3>
          SW SCHERER PARKWAY
        </h3>

        <div class="meta">
          Permit PRPWRW20240071
        </div>

        <p>
          3975 SW Scherer Pkwy.
          The permit describes placement of one solar-powered
          ALPR camera in Lee's Summit right-of-way on behalf
          of the Lee's Summit Police Department.
        </p>

        <a
          class="document-button"
          href="/documents/permits/scherer-pkwy-alpr-permit-2024.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          VIEW ORIGINAL PERMIT
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="document-card">

        <div class="date">
          JULY 19, 2024
        </div>

        <h3>
          SE 3RD STREET
        </h3>

        <div class="meta">
          Permit PRPWRW20243722
        </div>

        <p>
          300 SE 3rd St.
          The permit describes installation of one ALPR
          on a 12-foot pole.
        </p>

        <a
          class="document-button"
          href="/documents/permits/se-3rd-st-alpr-permit-2024.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          VIEW ORIGINAL PERMIT
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="document-card private">

        <div class="date">
          JUNE 26, 2024
        </div>

        <h3>
          WOODLAND SHORES
        </h3>

        <div class="meta">
          Permit PRPWRW20243264
        </div>

        <p>
          1705 NE Woodland Shores Ct.
          This permit states that the ALPR was being installed
          on behalf of the Woodland Shores Homeowners Association,
          rather than LSPD.
        </p>

        <a
          class="document-button"
          href="/documents/permits/woodland-shores-alpr-permit-2024.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          VIEW ORIGINAL PERMIT
        </a>

      </article>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<section class="record-section" id="money">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="record-label">
      RECORD 02
    </div>

    <h2>
      THE MONEY
    </h2>

    <p class="record-intro">
      The invoices and contract billing schedule show how Lee's Summit's
      Flock program was billed during the first year and what the recurring
      annual cost became afterward.
    </p>


    <div class="money-highlight">

      <div class="big-number">
        $909,150
      </div>

      <div class="big-number-label">
        TOTAL LISTED CONTRACT VALUE
      </div>

    </div>


    <div class="money-grid">

      <article class="money-card">

        <div class="date">
          AUGUST 30, 2023
        </div>

        <h3>
          FIRST PAYMENT
        </h3>

        <div class="money-amount">
          $121,650
        </div>

        <p>
          The first-year invoice includes 51 Falcon cameras,
          professional installation charges, Advanced Search,
          4 Falcon Flex units and 4 additional battery packs.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="money-card">

        <div class="date">
          OCTOBER 30, 2023
        </div>

        <h3>
          FIRST CAMERA VALIDATION
        </h3>

        <div class="money-amount">
          $43,750
        </div>

        <p>
          This invoice represents the next 25 percent of the first-year
          billing after the first camera installation and validation.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="money-card">

        <div class="date">
          APRIL 4, 2024
        </div>

        <h3>
          FINAL SYSTEM ACCEPTANCE
        </h3>

        <div class="money-amount">
          $43,750
        </div>

        <p>
          This invoice represents the final 25 percent of the first-year
          billing after final installation, validation and system acceptance.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="money-card featured-money">

        <div class="date">
          OCTOBER 29, 2024
        </div>

        <h3>
          YEAR 2 RECURRING COST
        </h3>

        <div class="money-amount">
          $175,000
        </div>

        <p>
          The invoice identifies this as Year 2 of the 60-month term.
          It includes 51 Falcon cameras, Advanced Search,
          4 Falcon Flex units and additional battery packs.
        </p>

      </article>

    </div>


    <div class="billing-summary">

      <h3>
        FIRST-YEAR BILLING
      </h3>

      <div class="billing-row">
        <span>At contract signing</span>
        <strong>$121,650</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="billing-row">
        <span>At first camera installation and validation</span>
        <strong>$43,750</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="billing-row">
        <span>At final system acceptance</span>
        <strong>$43,750</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="billing-row total-row">
        <span>YEAR 1 TOTAL</span>
        <strong>$209,150</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="billing-row recurring-row">
        <span>ANNUAL RECURRING AFTER YEAR 1</span>
        <strong>$175,000</strong>
      </div>

    </div>


    <div class="source-box">

      <h3>
        READ THE ORIGINAL RECORDS
      </h3>

      <p>
        The complete redacted invoice packet is available below.
        The contract billing schedule is also available in the full agreement.
      </p>

      <div class="source-buttons">

        <a
          class="document-button"
          href="/documents/flock-invoices-redacted.pdf"
