  </div>

</section>


<section class="record-section" id="contract">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="record-label">
      RECORD 03
    </div>

    <h2>
      THE CONTRACT
    </h2>

    <p class="record-intro">
      This is the complete agreement between the City of Lee's Summit
      and Flock Group Inc. The contract covers pricing, the term of the
      agreement, data use, retention, hardware ownership, installation,
      renewal and other operating terms.
    </p>


    <div class="contract-hero">

      <div>
        <div class="contract-small">
          AGREEMENT 2024-017
        </div>

        <div class="contract-total">
          $909,150
        </div>

        <div class="contract-total-label">
          LISTED CONTRACT TOTAL
        </div>
      </div>

      <a
        class="document-button contract-button"
        href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        READ THE FULL 56-PAGE CONTRACT
      </a>

    </div>


    <div class="contract-stats">

      <div class="contract-stat">
        <strong>60 MONTHS</strong>
        <span>INITIAL TERM</span>
      </div>

      <div class="contract-stat">
        <strong>24 MONTHS</strong>
        <span>RENEWAL TERM</span>
      </div>

      <div class="contract-stat">
        <strong>$175,000</strong>
        <span>ANNUAL RECURRING COST</span>
      </div>

      <div class="contract-stat">
        <strong>30 DAYS</strong>
        <span>STANDARD RETENTION</span>
      </div>

    </div>


    <div class="contract-findings">

      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 39
        </div>

        <h3>
          WHAT LEE'S SUMMIT BOUGHT
        </h3>

        <p>
          The Order Form lists 51 Falcon cameras, 4 Falcon Flex units,
          Advanced Search, additional battery packs and professional
          installation services.
        </p>

        <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf#page=39"
          target="_blank"
        >
          VIEW PAGE 39 →
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 40
        </div>

        <h3>
          HOW THE BILLING WORKS
        </h3>

        <p>
          Year 1 is divided into a $121,650 payment at signing,
          followed by two $43,750 payments tied to camera validation
          and final system acceptance. Annual recurring charges after
          Year 1 are listed at $175,000.
        </p>

        <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf#page=40"
          target="_blank"
        >
          VIEW PAGE 40 →
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 43
        </div>

        <h3>
          30 DAYS DOESN'T NECESSARILY ME GONE
        </h3>

        <p>
          The agreement says Flock deletes footage on a rolling
          30-day basis, while the City is responsible for extracting,
          downloading and archiving footage it wants to retain.
        </p>

        <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf#page=43"
          target="_blank"
        >
          VIEW PAGE 43 →
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 45
        </div>

        <h3>
          MORE THAN A LICENSE PLATE
        </h3>

        <p>
          The contract defines Vehicle Fingerprint as including
          attributes such as vehicle type, make, color, registration
          state, missing or covered plates, bumper stickers, decals,
          roof racks and bike racks.
        </p>

        <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf#page=45"
          target="_blank"
        >
          VIEW PAGE 45 →
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 48
        </div>

        <h3>
          WHO OWNS THE DATA
        </h3>

        <p>
          The agreement says Customer Data belongs to the Customer
          and that Flock does not own or sell that Customer Data.
          It also allows Flock to anonymize data and use the resulting
          anonymized data for purposes including machine-learning training.
        </p>

        <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/documents/flock-contract-2024-017.pdf#page=48"
          target="_blank"
        >
          VIEW PAGE 48 →
        </a>

      </article>


      <article class="contract-finding">

        <div class="date">
          PAGE 51
        </div>

        <h3>
          RENEWAL AND REMOVAL
        </h3>

        <p>
          The agreement provides for automatic renewal unless either
          party gives timely notice of non-renewal. It also states that
          Flock will remove applicable hardware after termination or expiration.
        </p>

        <a
