    <h2>
      VEHICLE FINGERPRINT
    </h2>

    <p class="record-intro">
      The contract makes clear that Flock's system is designed to capture
      more than a license plate number. It defines "Vehicle Fingerprint"
      as a collection of identifying vehicle characteristics.
    </p>


    <div class="feature-highlight">

      <div class="feature-label">
        CONTRACT PAGE 45
      </div>

      <h3>
        WHAT CAN BE CAPTURED?
      </h3>

      <div class="attribute-grid">

        <div class="attribute">VEHICLE TYPE</div>
        <div class="attribute">MAKE</div>
        <div class="attribute">COLOR</div>
        <div class="attribute">REGISTRATION STATE</div>
        <div class="attribute">MISSING / COVERED PLATES</div>
        <div class="attribute">BUMPER STICKERS</div>
        <div class="attribute">DECALS</div>
        <div class="attribute">ROOF RACKS</div>
        <div class="attribute">BIKE RACKS</div>

      </div>

    </div>


    <div class="explanation-grid">

      <div class="explanation-card">

        <div class="date">
          WHAT THE CONTRACT SAYS
        </div>

        <h3>
          IT IS NOT LIMITED TO THE PLATE
        </h3>

        <p>
          The agreement defines Vehicle Fingerprint as unique vehicular
          attributes captured through the service. Those attributes include
          vehicle type, make, color, registration state, missing or covered
          plates, bumper stickers, decals, roof racks and bike racks.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="explanation-card">

        <div class="date">
          WHY THIS MATTERS
        </div>

        <h3>
          A VEHICLE CAN BE SEARCHED BY CHARACTERISTICS
        </h3>

        <p>
          The contract describes a system capable of using identifying
          vehicle characteristics beyond the license plate itself.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>


